'' A TIE OVER UDT ARGUMENTS IS TKO0660, fbc's 98. Two conversion constructors (one with a
'' defaulted tail), the same with a tied second argument, a crossed pair (each overload exact
'' on one argument and a conversion on the other), and a UDT with a cast to each parameter
'' type. The tie report trusted only builtin and pointer arguments, so the first three said
'' nothing and the build stopped on TKO0994 (SemanticInfo.unbound) -- before fcf805427, the
'' first overload ran. A UDT argument now counts when its casts are all scored and no
'' candidate was refused on grounds the scoring does not model (overload.tiko ResolveCall_).
'' Lines 67, 69-71, 74 bind, as in fbc: a second argument breaks the tie, an exact type beats
'' a conversion, a nearer base beats a farther one, a base beats a conversion, a DT
'' constructor beats one from long.
''
'' MEASURED, fbc-modern 1.20 with -maxerr inf over the source: error 98 on lines 66, 68, 72,
'' 73 and nothing else (2026-11-23).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -fmax-errors 100 -c tests/diagnostics/src/overload-udt-tie.bas -o tests/diagnostics/src/overload-udt-tie.o
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: overload-udt-tie.bas(66,3): error TKO0660
'' EXPECT-OUT: overload-udt-tie.bas(68,3): error TKO0660
'' EXPECT-OUT: overload-udt-tie.bas(72,3): error TKO0660
'' EXPECT-OUT: overload-udt-tie.bas(73,3): error TKO0660
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0994
'' EXPECT-NOT: overload-udt-tie.bas(67,
'' EXPECT-NOT: overload-udt-tie.bas(69,
'' EXPECT-NOT: overload-udt-tie.bas(70,
'' EXPECT-NOT: overload-udt-tie.bas(71,
'' EXPECT-NOT: overload-udt-tie.bas(74,
'' EXPECT-MAX-DIAG: 4
